From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:48:35 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: macaudio: accept the read-back unlock state as a
 no-op

"Speaker Volume Unlock" reads back the lock state (0 or 1) but only
accepts the magic ping value on write and returns -EINVAL for anything
else. alsactl saves the read-back value and writes it back at boot.
When alsa-state restores the card before speakerguardd has taken the
lock on the control, the write reaches the put handler and fails, and
alsactl logs an error on every such boot:

  alsactl: set_control:1525: Cannot write control
  'numid=31,iface=MIXER,name='Speaker Volume Unlock'' : Invalid argument

The J616s hit this race on 66 of 236 boots over three days, and the
M1 Pro hits it too. When
the daemon wins the race the core rejects the write with -EPERM because
the control is locked, and our alsactl skips locked controls, so the
log stays clean.

Writing 0 or 1 back cannot change anything: the lease is renewed only
by the magic value from the lock owner. Treat those two values as a
no-op so that restoring a saved mixer state round-trips cleanly. Other
values still fail with -EINVAL, and the lock owner, magic value and
lease checks are unchanged, so nothing new can unlock the speaker
volumes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit e4698294d7a69439696aaee2212205ec67197711)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
index b366282f33..569cf80387 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
@@ -1886,8 +1886,18 @@ static int macaudio_slk_put(struct snd_kcontrol *kcontrol, struct snd_ctl_elem_v
 {
 	struct snd_soc_card *card = snd_kcontrol_chip(kcontrol);
 	struct macaudio_snd_data *ma = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(card);
+	long val = uvalue->value.integer.value[0];
 
-	if (uvalue->value.integer.value[0] != SPEAKER_MAGIC_VALUE)
+	/*
+	 * Reads return the lock state (0 or 1), so a saved mixer state holds
+	 * one of those. Writing it back changes nothing: only the lock owner's
+	 * magic value renews the lease. Accept it as a no-op so that restoring
+	 * a saved state before the daemon has taken the lock is not an error.
+	 */
+	if (val == 0 || val == 1)
+		return 0;
+
+	if (val != SPEAKER_MAGIC_VALUE)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	mutex_lock(&ma->volume_lock_mutex);
